{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Differential Attention (V2) Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements differential attention in pure Python. A toy query with known signal-plus-noise structure lets you measure the noise-cancellation ratio directly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: standard softmax attention"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Stdlib matrix ops: lists of lists, manual matmul, softmax with numerical-stability subtraction of the max."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def softmax(row):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    m = max(row)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exps = [math.exp(x - m) for x in row]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = sum(exps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [e / s for e in exps]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: split Q, K into two halves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "V1 style: halve the head dimension. V2 style: keep the head dimension and double the number of heads. The toy implementation uses V1 for pedagogical clarity \u2014 the math is identical, only the bookkeeping differs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: two softmax branches + subtraction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A1 = [softmax([dot(q1, k) / scale for k in K1]) for q1 in Q1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A2 = [softmax([dot(q2, k) / scale for k in K2]) for q2 in Q2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "diff_weights = [[a1 - lam * a2 for a1, a2 in zip(r1, r2)] for r1, r2 in zip(A1, A2)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "out = [[sum(w * v[j] for w, v in zip(row, V)) for j in range(d_v)] for row in diff_weights]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Note: the output weights can be negative. That is fine \u2014 the value cache still handles signed contributions. The subsequent V projection absorbs the sign."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: noise cancellation measurement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Build a synthetic sequence of length 1024. Place the signal token at a known position, fill the rest with noise. Compute (a) standard softmax attention weight on the signal position and (b) differential attention weight. Measure the ratio of signal-to-noise in each. DIFF attention reliably produces a higher signal-to-noise ratio by a factor of 3x-10x depending on how much the two branches have been trained to differ."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: V1 vs V2 parameter accounting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Given a config (hidden=4096, heads=32, d_head=128), print:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Baseline Transformer: Q, K, V each size `hidden * hidden`, MLP at 4 * hidden."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- DIFF V1: Q, K each size `hidden * hidden`, V size `hidden * hidden` (unchanged), head dim halved internally. Adds per-head `lambda` parameters (O(heads * d_head))."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- DIFF V2: Q size `2 * hidden * hidden`, K size `hidden * hidden`, V size `hidden * hidden`. Extra dim projected back down before O_W. Adds same `lambda` parameters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The toy measures the extra parameter cost for V2 (roughly `hidden * hidden` extra per attention block) and prints it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Run `code/main.py`. Verify the signal-to-noise ratio reported for differential attention is higher than standard softmax attention on the synthetic query. Vary the noise amplitude and show the crossover point where standard attention becomes unusable.\n\n2. Compute the parameter-count delta from baseline to DIFF V1 and from baseline to DIFF V2 for a 7B-class model (hidden=4096, heads=32, d_head=128, 32 layers). Show which components gained parameters and which stayed the same.\n\n3. Read Section 3 of the DIFF V1 paper (arXiv:2410.05258) and Section 2 of the DIFF V2 Hugging Face blog. In two sentences, explain why the V1 per-head RMSNorm was necessary and why V2 could remove it without causing training divergence.\n\n4. Implement an ablation: compute differential attention with `lambda = 0` (pure first softmax) and `lambda = 1` (full subtraction). On the synthetic query, measure how signal-to-noise changes across the sweep. Identify the `lambda` that maximizes signal-to-noise.\n\n5. Extend the toy to GQA + DIFF V2. Pick 8 KV heads and 32 Q heads. Show that the KV cache size matches a baseline GQA model with the same (8, 32) configuration."
      ]
    }
  ],
